{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 179825, "name": "James bond", "username": "bond", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/bond/{size}/2164_2.png", "created_at": "2021-08-28T14:12:21.748Z", "cooked": "<p><em>Disclaimer: Curiosity. Ultra noob trying to know what, why &amp; how.</em></p>\n<p>Is it okay to purge this package? Is there any need for this package? What does it do anyway?<br>\n<img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/c/5/c53e8160ea8ac07b303830183c26250922e64727.png\" alt=\"6ff604ac2f58f52d123b1861a5ab468b158beb4d.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"s8TYGGYjUY70VdddEpB6eaPLdJl\" width=\"565\" height=\"108\"></p>\n<p>When I tried to reinstall it, it showed a download size of <strong>669 MB</strong>! It’s a lot. Maybe it has some importance. Then why does the flatpak list it as an unused package? Shouldn’t the “important” package be at least used once?!<br>\n<div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/a/1/a1cd3cd50b2e0cd612c8e34734d53ab664daec0e.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/n5mAIUfpgnnjYYwgQPu34ZUS3ue.png?dl=1\" title=\"ec3a2884bcc83dba6ed621762222a6bd0d6a4323.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"><img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/optimized/3X/a/1/a1cd3cd50b2e0cd612c8e34734d53ab664daec0e_2_690x120.png\" alt=\"ec3a2884bcc83dba6ed621762222a6bd0d6a4323.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"n5mAIUfpgnnjYYwgQPu34ZUS3ue\" width=\"690\" height=\"120\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/optimized/3X/a/1/a1cd3cd50b2e0cd612c8e34734d53ab664daec0e_2_690x120.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/a/1/a1cd3cd50b2e0cd612c8e34734d53ab664daec0e.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/a/1/a1cd3cd50b2e0cd612c8e34734d53ab664daec0e.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"41434E\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">ec3a2884bcc83dba6ed621762222a6bd0d6a4323.png</span><span class=\"informations\">978×171 24.6 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>After the Branch, there is a label called <strong>Op</strong>. What does this mean? When I remove this package, it said <code>Op= r</code>, and later when I installed the package, it said <code>Op= i</code>. What it’s trying to say?</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2023-06-22T16:38:53.593Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 429, "reads": 29, "readers_count": 28, "score": 2170.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77864, "topic_slug": "flatpak-uninstall-unused-command-shows-org-fedoraproject-platform-as-unused-669-mb-package-is-it-okay-to-uninstall-it", "display_username": "James bond", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 4, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/a/1/a1cd3cd50b2e0cd612c8e34734d53ab664daec0e.png", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "a1cd3cd50b2e0cd612c8e34734d53ab664daec0e.png", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 2085, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/flatpak-uninstall-unused-command-shows-org-fedoraproject-platform-as-unused-669-mb-package-is-it-okay-to-uninstall-it/77864/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 203196, "name": "dalto", "username": "dalto", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/dalto/{size}/5564_2.png", "created_at": "2021-08-28T14:17:57.127Z", "cooked": "<p>It is the runtime for Fedora flatpaks.  If you don’t have any of the flatpaks that depend on that installed, it will be unused.</p>\n<p>It is more or less always safe to remove flatpaks.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"bond\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"77864\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/bond/48/2164_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bond:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>After the Branch, there is a label called <strong>Op</strong> . What does this mean? When I remove this package, it said <code>Op= r</code> , and later when I installed the package, it said <code>Op= i</code> . What it’s trying to say?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>r for <strong>r</strong>emove and i for <strong>i</strong>nstall.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"bond\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"77864\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/bond/48/2164_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bond:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>When I tried to reinstall it, it showed a download size of <strong>669 MB</strong> ! It’s a lot.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Flatpak runtimes are typically fairly large. That is normal.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2023-03-08T22:48:17.884Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 8, "reads": 29, "readers_count": 28, "score": 65.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77864, "topic_slug": "flatpak-uninstall-unused-command-shows-org-fedoraproject-platform-as-unused-669-mb-package-is-it-okay-to-uninstall-it", "display_username": "dalto", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 3609, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/flatpak-uninstall-unused-command-shows-org-fedoraproject-platform-as-unused-669-mb-package-is-it-okay-to-uninstall-it/77864/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": true, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 119499, "name": "James bond", "username": "bond", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/bond/{size}/2164_2.png", "created_at": "2021-08-28T15:16:15.238Z", "cooked": "<p>Something new happen this time when I used the same command.</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/d/3/d3521e5ac6012df36c55f0c388741e7c9834c129.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/u9qGrclLGQy3Z7r1N4tJmIYUJAZ.png?dl=1\" title=\"fccd591dada0969542f38c78e11b92e415a5b907.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"><img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/d/3/d3521e5ac6012df36c55f0c388741e7c9834c129.png\" alt=\"fccd591dada0969542f38c78e11b92e415a5b907.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"u9qGrclLGQy3Z7r1N4tJmIYUJAZ\" width=\"690\" height=\"97\" data-dominant-color=\"484A53\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">fccd591dada0969542f38c78e11b92e415a5b907.png</span><span class=\"informations\">836×118 15.9 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>Someone in the power to make this change read this post and did something about it. Cool.</p>\n<p>Thanks for all the other info you mentioned.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2023-03-09T07:23:16.528Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 7, "reads": 26, "readers_count": 25, "score": 70.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77864, "topic_slug": "flatpak-uninstall-unused-command-shows-org-fedoraproject-platform-as-unused-669-mb-package-is-it-okay-to-uninstall-it", "display_username": "James bond", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/d/3/d3521e5ac6012df36c55f0c388741e7c9834c129.png", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "d3521e5ac6012df36c55f0c388741e7c9834c129.png", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 3295, "username": "jimbo2150", "name": "Jim", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/disc